                    </Grid>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource Note}" x:Name="DragVerdict"/>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource Note}"
                               Text="Trap speed and elapsed time are not equally worth trusting. By the far end a car has had a quarter of a mile to forget a bad launch, so the speed it arrives at is very nearly a measure of power against weight. The time does not forget — a wheelspin in the first sixty feet is in it for good. So the trap is read for power, and the time is read for the start line."/>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource Note}"
                               Text="These are correlations fitted to thousands of real runs, not physics. There is no term here for traction, gearing, the air, the track or the driver — any of which moves a quarter-mile time by more than the differences between the three formulas. Every figure is the middle of a wide distribution."/>
                </StackPanel>
